  "description": "HW-391 2S (7.4 V nominal / 8.4 V full) 20 A lithium-ion protection board with balancing, 48 x 20 mm, five through-hole solder pads. Drawing = TOP (component) side, as in the listing's orthographic top view: the 4.2V balance-tap pad at the middle of the LEFT short edge with the P- (silkscreen minus-in-circle) and P+ (plus-in-circle) pads just right of it, 0V at the top-right corner, 8.4V at the bottom-right corner, the four DPAK MOSFETs in the right half, the two 430 shunt resistors along the bottom edge. Wiring: 0V = cell-1 minus (B-), 4.2V = cell-1 plus / cell-2 minus junction (B1, balance tap), 8.4V = cell-2 plus (B+), P- / P+ = charger and load. 8.4V and P+ are one copper pour on the back side (bused); 0V and P- are separated by the MOSFETs (not bused). Board size from the listing's dimension callout; pad positions measured on the orthographic photo (estimated, about +/-0.3 mm).",
